WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.831
What’s up everybody, my name is Ohara and
today we’re gonna talk about the man, the

00:00:04.831 --> 00:00:09.639
myth, the legend, Red Hair Shanks and his
purpose in the story of One Piece.

00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:15.599
I think it’s pretty fair to say that Shanks
is one of THE most liked and widely celebrated

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:18.869
characters in the entirety of the One Piece
story.

00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:24.410
In all 6 popularity polls that were conducted
until today, Shanks always easily placed within

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:32.320
at LEAST the top 15 . To put this into perspective,
on average Shanks is MORE popular than Usopp,

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:39.220
Brook or Franky, all of which have been an
active part of the story for hundreds of chapters.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:44.850
Shanks meanwhile is mentioned in less than
30 chapters, and appears in less than 15.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.350
15 CHAPTERS!

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.560
Out of roughly a THOUSAND.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.770
Let that sink in for a moment.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:56.170
However, despite his lack of screen-time,
it’s relatively easy to see WHAT makes Shanks

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:01.930
so fascinating: Oda portrays the Yonko as
a charismatic leader that, despite his goofy

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:07.270
and often easy-going nature, is respected
and feared throughout the world and is one

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:10.030
of its MOST influential players.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:15.020
At the same time, the quite rare occasions
his name is dropped and the even RARER appearances

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:20.720
he actually has, shroud his character in a
sense of mystery and uncertainty.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:26.100
This EXTREMLY appealing character design has
lead to countless theories over Shanks’

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.210
true role in the story: Is he actually a Celestial
Dragon?

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.670
Will he die at the hands of Blackbeard?

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:37.280
Or will he ultimately turn out to be the main
villain of the story, after all?

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.840
What will this mysterious and legendary pirate,
that we have known since the very first chapter

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.380
of the story, actually be doing in the end?

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:48.120
In this video, we will answer ALL of these
questions.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:53.100
Because, if you look closely enough at how
Oda is placing Shanks in the story, it becomes

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:58.280
clear that the Yonko is presented as something
that you could call the secret guarding of

00:01:58.280 --> 00:01:59.950
the One Piece world.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:05.410
This can be seen in his strikingly pacifistic
nature, his unique and inherent goodness among

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:11.260
the Yonko as well as in his undeniable ties
to nordic mythology and lore.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:15.250
Once we have looked at these three factors,
at the end of this video, we will be able

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.760
to see CLEARLY what role Shanks actually plays
in the story.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:27.370
So grab yourself some coffee, we have to talk
about Akagami no Shankusu.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:32.150
When you hear the word pacifist, the first
thing you probably think about in the context

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:36.379
of One Piece are the Pacifista created by
Dr. Vegapunk.

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:41.669
However, when we look at the definition of
pacifism, it becomes relatively clear that

00:02:41.669 --> 00:02:46.030
something went horribly wrong with the World
Government´s naming scheme here.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:51.790
Because a pacifist per definition, is a person
who believes that unnecessary war and violence

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.939
are unjustifiable.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:57.780
Not exactly fitting when you look at this.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.459
Now with Shanks on the other hand, this is
a completely different story.

00:03:02.459 --> 00:03:07.809
He is a true pacifist, that tries to avoid
unnecessary conflict and violence if in any

00:03:07.809 --> 00:03:09.310
way possible.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:13.540
This is even acknowledged by the Gorosei,
who state that he is not the type of person

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.659
that seeks chaos and disorder.

00:03:15.659 --> 00:03:20.620
However, that doesn’t mean of course that
Shanks does not enjoy some friendly sparring

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:25.499
here and then, as he clearly does with Mihawk
or against the Whiteboard pirates as a rookie

00:03:25.499 --> 00:03:27.040
on Roger´s ship.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:33.181
However, compared to most other pirates, and
similarly to Luffy, Shanks has no interest

00:03:33.181 --> 00:03:35.870
in pointless cruelty or bloodshed.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:41.370
But I believe that it goes even further than
this: Shanks seems to have an active interest

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:45.409
in keeping the quite fragile balance of the
one piece world.

00:03:45.409 --> 00:03:50.540
This becomes clear when he steps in to stop
the war at marine-ford or whenever he expresses

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.980
his worries about Blackbeard.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:58.519
In this context, one of Shanks’ most stunning
skills that he rarely gets any credit for,

00:03:58.519 --> 00:04:01.840
is his deep understanding of diplomacy.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:07.040
None other than Shanks is able to stop a war
between the Marines and another Yonko or get

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:12.029
a private audience with the Gorosei, all while
being one of the most notorious criminals

00:04:12.029 --> 00:04:13.129
on the planet.

00:04:13.129 --> 00:04:18.410
But we can see this sort of de-escalating
and effective diplomacy in other instances

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:19.620
as well.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:23.580
For example his meeting with Whiteboard to
discuss the danger of Blackbeard.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:29.030
Or his notoriously forgiving attitude towards
Higuma, a mere mountain bandit from the east

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:32.370
blue that tried to humiliate him in front
of his men.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:37.680
And maybe, he even managed to find a diplomatic
solution in his encounter with Kaido, where

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:43.319
he somehow managed to stop the Yonko from
going after Whitebeard and afterwards arrives

00:04:43.319 --> 00:04:48.430
at Marienford without so much as a scratch.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:55.030
What all these examples clearly show us however,
is how averse Shanks truly is to unjust bloodshed

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:56.900
and unnecessary violence.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:03.360
However, as we all know just too well, Shanks
also has another side.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:08.250
Whenever his ideals and values are being threatened,
Shanks is ready to take up arms and deliver

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.010
Justice.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:15.580
Notoriously of course, we can see this, once
Higuma takes things too far and kidnaps and

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.330
threatens Luffy.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:22.389
When arriving at Marineford, Shanks is prepared
to face Akainu and the Marines heads on, should

00:05:22.389 --> 00:05:27.060
they refuse to lay down their weapons, and
everyone is more than reluctant to test him

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.410
and his crew.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:32.490
This could even have played a role in his
encounter with Kid, where the Supernova lost

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:34.330
an arm to the Yonko.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:40.389
Given his character, it is entirely possible
that Kid did something SO unjust or cruel,

00:05:40.389 --> 00:05:44.050
that Shanks saw it necessary to bestow justice
upon him.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:50.259
This striking duality of diplomatic pacifism
and unwavering justice are a defining part

00:05:50.259 --> 00:05:52.150
of Shanks’ character.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:56.780
But to truly understand this unique position
of his in the world of one piece, we of course

00:05:56.780 --> 00:06:02.050
also have to understand his equally unique
standing among the Yonko.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:08.280
There are number of things that make Shanks
the odd one out when it comes to his membership

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:11.960
within the 4 strongest and most feared pirates.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:16.710
For instance, as far as we know, he is the
only one of the four that is not commanding

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:18.270
an entire fleet.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:22.780
And we are also yet to come across any island
that stands under his protection or rule.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:28.259
Also, Shanks is the only one that evidently
has not eaten any devil fruit.

00:06:28.259 --> 00:06:33.430
And weirdly enough he is also the only one,
not associated with the rocks pirates in any

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:39.310
way, with Big Mom and Kaido being former members,
and Blackbeard having served on Whitebeards

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:43.490
crew as well as naming his ship after him.

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:48.490
This already tells us quite a lot about him,
as he is also the only Yonko that has never

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:54.360
opposed Luffy and has no interest in gaining
more power nor in becoming pirate king.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:59.319
In more than just one way, it doesn’t take
a lot of deep analysis to come to the conclusion

00:06:59.319 --> 00:07:04.789
that Shanks is the only emperor that can be
considered to be “good” at this point

00:07:04.789 --> 00:07:06.090
in the story.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:10.509
He was the one inspiring Luffy to become a
pirate and setting out to see, believing that

00:07:10.509 --> 00:07:14.190
he will be the one to change the world one
day for the better.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:18.689
His attempts to keep Blackbeard and Kaido
at bay suggest to us that Shanks sees himself

00:07:18.689 --> 00:07:23.540
as a sort of counterweight to the other Yonko
to maintain stability in the world.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:28.870
Using his power and staying true to his theme
of war and justice, Shanks works to protect

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:34.010
the world, by ensuring a stability and balance
between all the forces at work there.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:38.879
Whether he does so to even the way for Luffy
or to follow some other objective, we will

00:07:38.879 --> 00:07:40.159
have to wait and see.

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:45.389
However, Oda might have left us a couple of
hints towards what Shanks’ storyline is

00:07:45.389 --> 00:07:46.919
moving toward.

00:07:46.919 --> 00:07:54.039
And these hints can be found in the close
connection that he has to nordic mythology.

00:07:54.039 --> 00:07:59.889
In nordic mythology there exists the legend
of Týr, the god of war and justice, that

00:07:59.889 --> 00:08:02.860
once ruled over the other gods before Odin.

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:08.639
When the giant wolf Fenrir, son of Loki, was
prophesied to kill Odin, the gods took him

00:08:08.639 --> 00:08:11.979
to Agard and attempted to bind and control
him.

00:08:11.979 --> 00:08:17.159
Fenrir however, whom they told it would be
a mere test of his strength, would only permit

00:08:17.159 --> 00:08:22.080
them to put the chains on him if one of them
would be willing to put their arm between

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.590
his fangs as insurance.

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:30.259
None of the gods was willing to do so, except
for Tyr, who strode forward and placed his

00:08:30.259 --> 00:08:32.380
arm in the wolf’s mouth.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:37.720
Once Fenrir had realised that he could not
escape, he bit off Tyr´s arm, who thus managed

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:41.220
to uphold justice and order at the same time.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.210
Does this sound familiar yet?

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.690
However the similarities do not end here.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:50.780
Shanks and Tyr both are renowned for their
swordsmanship, their sense of justice, as

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.260
well as their red hair.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:55.410
And not for nothing does Shanks sail on a
Viking Ship.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:09:00.410
I think it’s pretty likely that Oda has
borrowed at least SOME inspiration for Shanks’

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:03.570
character from this nordic god.

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:08.950
Interestingly enough, Tyr has been prophesied
to be killed by Gramr at Ragnarok, the great

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:11.370
battle to end the era of the gods.

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:16.560
Garmr is a huge hell-hound, often depicted
with three heads.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:19.030
I think you know where I’m going with this.

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:23.850
Blackbeard and Shanks have long been set up
to clash at some point in the future and there

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:27.130
simply are a lot of striking similarities
here.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:31.870
Shanks was the first one to take Blackbeard
very seriously very early on.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:36.030
He already noticed something strange about
him when they first met as apprentices on

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:38.030
Roger´s and Whitebeard´s ship.

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:43.030
He later encountered him again at some point,
where he was dealt the scar across his eyes.

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:50.400
And finally he is the one to urge WB and possibly
even the Gorosei to take Teach seriously.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:54.380
Thematicly, this storyline would fit perfectly.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:59.680
We ALSO know, that Elbaf, is heavily inspired
my nordic culture and mythology as well, with

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.220
all the viking themes going around there.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:07.350
And when we meet the very first giants in
the story on Little Garden, Dorry and Broggy,

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:13.030
they say the following to Usopp: “When there's
a dispute and neither side will yield...The

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:15.040
god of Elbaf decides the matter.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:19.120
Our god protects the one who is right...and
lets him live.”

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:24.980
Could Shanks possibly not only be inspired
by the god of war and justice, but be considered

